# Course statuses (two fields)

Do not collapse these into one value.

| Field | Meaning | Values |
|-------|---------|--------|
| `status` | Overall lifecycle | `draft` until submit; then `active` (or `published` / `archived`) |
| `is_active` | Active / Not active toggle on the editor | boolean (`true` / `false`) |

## Rules

- **Save as draft** writes `status: draft`. It must not copy the activity dropdown into `status`.
- **Submit / Save** writes `status: active` (keep `published`/`archived` if already set). Activity still goes only to `is_active`.
- Never set `status` from `is_active` (or the reverse) in list/detail/editor mapping.
- After **Save as draft**, stay on the editor (replace `/courses/:id/edit` on first create). Do not bounce to the list.
- After **Submit / إرسال**, go to the courses list (`/courses` or `/standalone-courses`).
- Delete remains draft-only (`status === 'draft'`).
- Schedule **Add class** subject dropdowns list **all course kinds** (milestone / graded / standalone) that pass `isCourseSchedulable`: submitted (`active`/`published`) **and** Active (`is_active`), **and** whose `level_id` matches the selected group’s fee level (`group.level_id`). When editing, the currently saved course stays listed even if levels no longer match.
- Payment **Course fees** list (`/settings/payments/courses`) and fee-package course pickers use the same rule.

```ts
// BAD — drafts with is_active=true show as Active
status: course.is_active ? 'active' : 'inactive'

// GOOD
status: courseLifecycleStatus(course) // draft | active | published | archived
is_active: course.is_active !== false
```

Helpers: `school-management-unified/src/utils/course-status.ts`.
